% =============================================================================
%  refs.bib -- the bibliography database for cse200-demo.tex
% =============================================================================
%  Cite these keys from the .tex with \cite{...} / \citep{...} / \citet{...},
%  then pull the list in with:
%      \bibliographystyle{unsrtnat}
%      \bibliography{refs}          <-- the file name, WITHOUT ".bib"
%
%  Compile order: pdflatex -> bibtex -> pdflatex -> pdflatex
%  (or just: latexmk -pdf cse200-demo.tex)
%
%  ENTRY TYPES you are likely to need (each is written with a leading "at"
%  sign in a real entry -- omitted here because BibTeX would try to parse them
%  even inside a comment):
%      book          author, title, publisher, year   (+ edition, address)
%      article       author, title, journal, year     (+ volume, number, pages, doi)
%      inproceedings author, title, booktitle, year   (+ pages, publisher)
%      techreport    author, title, institution, year
%      misc          author, title, year, howpublished, note, url
%      phdthesis     author, title, school, year
%
%  GOTCHAS
%    - A stray "at" sign anywhere in this file, even in a comment, makes
%      BibTeX try to read an entry and emit "I'm skipping whatever remains"
%    - An ampersand inside a field must be escaped: John Wiley \& Sons
%    - Accents:  Rapha\"el   Acad\'emie   G\"odel
%    - To stop BibTeX lowercasing a word in a title, brace it: {DNA}
%    - The key (the first thing after the brace) is what you type in \cite{}
%      and it is case-sensitive.
% =============================================================================

